---
import MarketingPage from '../../layouts/MarketingPage.astro';
import { CTA, DOCS } from '../../lib/site';
---

<MarketingPage
  title="GitHub App · openpreflight"
  description="Install a GitHub App you own, bind a repo, and get the first Check Run. How-to lives in the docs."
>
  <p class="kicker"><a href="/integrations/">Integrations</a> / GitHub App</p>
  <h1>Install, bind, first Check Run</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    openpreflight does not create the App for you. You register it, paste the
    PEM and webhook secret into the UI, enable a binding, and push.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Register the App with the permissions and events in the docs.</li>
    <li>Point the webhook at <code>https://your-host/webhook/&#123;slug&#125;</code>.</li>
    <li>Install the App on the org or repos you care about.</li>
    <li>Enable a binding. Push a commit (or open a PR).</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The full checklist, permission table, and event list:
    <a href={`${DOCS}/setup/github-app/`}>Register a GitHub App</a>.
    Bindings:
    <a href={`${DOCS}/setup/bindings/`}>enable repos</a>.
  </p>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a class="primary" href={`${DOCS}/setup/github-app/`}>Setup docs</a>
    <a class="secondary" href={CTA.quickstart}>Quickstart</a>
  </div>
</MarketingPage>
